FELIXBAS.EXE: Felix BASIC, a GW-BASIC/QBasic-style interpreter with a full
screen editor, graphics (SCREEN, PSET, LINE, CIRCLE, PAINT, ...) and sound
(SOUND, PLAY, BEEP on the PC speaker). On C: only, in its own folder
C:\VMDOS\BASIC (with this file as README.TXT and its license); BASIC.BAT in
C:\VMDOS, on the PATH, starts it. The boot floppy has no room for it.

It is the MS-DOS build of wopr/wopr_basic from
github.com/jasonbrianhall/felixterminal (wopr/wopr_basic/msdos; MIT license,
LICENSE.md here), built with DJGPP (32-bit, so it runs under vmdos's DPMI
host, like LESS, VIM and FSCK) with the plain DJGPP stub instead of
CWSDPMI's, and packed with UPX. Unmodified.

  BASIC                 the editor (F5 runs, F6 the Ok prompt, F1 help)
  BASIC PROG.BAS        run PROG.BAS and exit
  BASIC -e PROG.BAS     open PROG.BAS in the editor
  BASIC -c              start at the Ok prompt (EDIT goes to the editor)
  BASIC -h              help

Video: VESA 640x480 in more than 16 colours when there is one, else VGA
mode 12h; SET FELIXVID=800x600x16 picks another mode, SET FELIXFPS=30 the
frame rate (1-200).

Rebuild: tools/build-felixbasic.sh (Docker, or a local DJGPP; upx; FELIXSRC=checkout
or a fresh clone of felixterminal, REF=branch/tag). Every night
.github/workflows/felixbasic.yml checks felixterminal and, when its BASIC has
changed, rebuilds and opens a pull request (branch felixbasic-update).
Built from (felixterminal commit, date, source id; the script keeps this line):
felixterminal b0ba7cf 2026-11-13 source 3cd28963c450
